          1408.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "438b9c7fd92cafb046d81980f4032cf7d281f7967189027eff11f1167338dee5"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $\\partial L/\\partial \\boldsymbol{\\Theta}$ is a column vector of the partials of the log-likelihood function with respect to each parameter evaluated at the estimate $\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}^{(k)}$, and $\\mathbf{H}$ is the Hessian matrix of all second-order partial derivatives of the log-likelihood L with respect to the variance components. $ \\mathbf{H}^{-1} $ and $ \\partial L/\\partial \\Theta $ respectively provide measures of the curvature and the slope (and directionality) of the likelihood surface, given the current estimates. Their product gives a projected degree of movement of the vector $ \\Theta $ towards an improved set of values to be used in the next iteration.",
      "source_page": 806,
      "printed_page": 786,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter27:p016:b10",
        "Genetics_chapter27:p017:b2"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        184.0,
        1442.0,
        1144.0,
        1543.0
      ],
      "source_page_end": 807,
      "source_pages": [
        806,
        807
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
