    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $\\mathbf{u}_i \\sim \\text{MVN}(\\mathbf{0}, \\sigma_i^2 \\mathbf{B}_i)$ for $1 \\leq i \\leq m$, and $\\mathbf{B}_i$ is a square symmetric $n_i \\times n_i$ matrix of known constants. The residuals are also assumed to be multivariate normal with $\\mathbf{e} \\sim \\text{MVN}(\\mathbf{0}, \\sigma_E^2 \\mathbf{I})$. Since $\\mathbf{y}$ is the sum of multivariate normals, it is also multivariate normal with $\\mathbf{y} \\sim \\text{MVN}(\\mathbf{X}\\boldsymbol{\\beta}, \\mathbf{V})$, where",
      "source_page": 807,
      "printed_page": 787,
      "source_block_ids": [
